      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As you know, floats take up 8 bits of space in your parameters with a range of -1 to 1, meaning there are only 255 possible values. \nIn vrchat's case, floats have 254 possible values, as being able to divide 254 into 2 parts of 127 allows for the values -1, 0 and 1 to be quantized cleanly. As such you can think of floats having a range of -1 to 1 with increments of 1/127.\nYour value of 0.2 is represented as floor(127 * 0.2) / 127 = 0.1968503937007874",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
