  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-29T15:24:00.310Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Short: \nFloat-Values are different locally and remotely, when synced via Expression Parameters.\nWhat I did:\nI used the VRC Parameter Driver and I add 0.1 or any other Float\n(See Screenshot).\nThen I sync up the value by putting it into the expression parameters.\nLocally the Value is 0.1, \nbut on remote systems it is not the same value.\nI tested it multiple times, \nwhen the value should be 0.2 (it was for me), it was around 0.19685 for a friend of mine and so on. And smaller numbers ar even worse, which is understandable, if using a smol amount of bits.\nSo it might be a floating point precision issue, where the value gets screwed over networking. \nOr it is something else I cannot think of right now.\nThanks in Advance.",
